   Independent-implementation statement (UoT).
   The UDP-over-TCP (UoT) files above implement the SAME ON-THE-WIRE PROTOCOL
   as sing-box / the sagernet/sing library (GPL-3.0), so that the two
   interoperate. They are NOT a derivative work of that GPL-3.0 code:

     - A wire format / network protocol is a method of operation and is not
       protected by copyright; anyone may implement it independently.
     - These files are an original, from-scratch C++ implementation. Their
       structure and expression differ substantially from the Go original:
       the Go code uses blocking sequential reads (binary.Read / io.ReadFull)
       and delegates address coding to a shared serializer
       (M.SocksaddrSerializer / uot.AddrParser); this implementation uses an
       explicit incremental state machine (NaiveUotFramer::Feed with a
       ReadState enum) and its own hand-written address codecs. No source code
       was copied or translated.
     - References to sing-box type names in code comments are interoperability
       documentation only (describing the wire bytes to match); they do not
       incorporate any GPL-3.0 source.

   Accordingly these files are licensed under BSD-3-Clause and the GPL-3.0 of
   sing-box / sagernet/sing does not extend to them.

